Day 27: Simple Text-Based Inventory System

Concepts used:
 dictionary with numeric values,
 combining everything from Days 20-26 (menus, dicts, validation)

Problem Statement

Write a Python program that manages a shop's inventory using a dictionary: {item_name: quantity}. Menu:
1. Add New Item
2. Restock Item (increase quantity)
3. Sell Item (decrease quantity)
4. View Inventory
5. Low Stock Alert (items with quantity < 5)
6. Exit

Things to handle
   i)Add New Item: if the item already exists, warn the user instead of overwriting (different from Day 21's contact book — here, be strict).
  ii)Restock: item must already exist; increase its quantity by the entered amount.
 iii)Sell: item must exist AND have enough stock — don't allow selling more than what's in stock (print "Not enough stock" instead).
  iv)Low Stock Alert: loop through inventory, print any item with quantity < 5.

